# Cribl-Microsoft Repository .gitignore
# ===========================================

# Testing files to ignore
# ============================================
# `dev/`, not `dev*`: unanchored `dev*` also matched every Device*.json ARM
# template, and on Windows/macOS (core.ignorecase=true) `git add` dropped them
# while still exiting 0. Directory form keeps Dev/ and */dev/ ignored.
dev/
.dev-mode
# CLAUDE.md is TRACKED. The old rules here were `*claude*`, `*Cluade*` and
# `*CLAUDE*`, unanchored, and they hid the file that tells every contributor
# and every agent how this repo works - a fresh clone got no project
# instructions at all. See the .claude/ exception under Dot Directories below;
# this is the third unanchored pattern here to hide something it never meant
# to (compare `dev*` above and the DCR-Automation rules below).
knowledge.md

# Backup configuration files
*.backup.json
*-backup.json
*.bak

# DCR Automation generated output (regenerated on every deployment)
#
# Matched from any depth rather than anchored at the repo root. The root-anchored
# form silently stopped matching when Azure/ moved under deprecated/ on
# 2026-07-13, which is how a credentials-bearing azure-parameters.json became
# tracked. These rules must survive the next move too.
**/DCR-Automation/core/generated-templates/
**/DCR-Automation/core/cribl-dcr-configs/
**/DCR-Automation/dev/generated-templates/
**/DCR-Automation/dev/cribl-dcr-configs/

# User-specific config (contains credentials and selections). Any prefix, any
# depth: core/, dev/, prod/, dev-azure-parameters.json, devsan_azure-parameters
# .json - the dev-prefixed ones were previously ignored only as a side effect of
# `dev*`, so narrowing that rule would have exposed them.
**/*azure-parameters.json
**/DCR-Automation/*/NativeTableList.json
**/DCR-Automation/*/CustomTableList.json


# Test output and results
test-results/
regression-test-results/
*-test-output/

# =======================
# Temporary and Cache Files
# =======================
# Temporary PowerShell files
*.tmp
*.temp
*.cache

# PowerShell execution logs
*.log
*.out

# Log directories
logs/
**/logs/
# But keep SOURCE directories named "logs" (the SOC toolkit's diagnostics
# viewer lives in packages/ui/src/screens/logs; runtime log data is under
# apps/local-app/data/, ignored by that app's own .gitignore)
!soc-optimizationtoolkit/packages/ui/src/screens/logs/

# Temporary marker files
.cribl-collection-in-progress
.automation-in-progress
.*-marker

# =======================
# Dot Directories (Hidden)
# =======================
# All hidden directories starting with dot
.*/
# ...except .claude/, which holds this repo's own working agreements rather
# than a personal editor cache: the hooks enforcing the audit cadence, the
# docs-drift check and the board-freshness check. A correction to one of them
# on 2026-08-27 could not be committed, which is what prompted this.
!.claude/
# Personal, machine-specific - Claude Code's own convention is that
# settings.json is shared and settings.local.json is not.
.claude/settings.local.json
# Most skills here are symlinked in from claude-kit and re-pulled rather than
# maintained in this repo, so they are ignored by default.
#
# The exceptions are the skills this repo OWNS - they encode working agreements
# specific to it and are useless anywhere else, so they must travel with a
# clone. architecture-audit was tracked before this rule existed and survived
# only because gitignore does not untrack what is already in the index;
# backlog-grooming hit the rule head-on and had to be let through explicitly.
#
# Note the `/*`: excluding `.claude/skills/` itself would make the negations
# below unreachable, because git cannot re-include a file whose parent
# directory is excluded.
.claude/skills/*
!.claude/skills/architecture-audit/
!.claude/skills/backlog-grooming/
.vscode/
.vs/
.idea/

# PowerShell module cache
.psmodules/

# Azure CLI cache
.azure/

# Configuration directories
.config/
.settings/

# =======================
# Platform-Specific Files
# =======================
# Windows
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/
*.lnk

# macOS
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
Icon?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes

# Linux
*~
.nfs*

# =======================
# Development Tools
# =======================
# Visual Studio Code
.vscode/
*.code-workspace

# Visual Studio
.vs/
*.user
*.suo
*.userosscache
*.sln.docstates

# JetBrains IDEs
.idea/
*.iml
*.ipr
*.iws

# PowerShell ISE
*.psprojects

# =======================
# Documentation Build
# =======================
# Documentation generators
_site/
.jekyll-cache/
.sass-cache/

# =======================
# Package Managers
# =======================
# Node.js
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
# package-lock.json must be committed so all users get identical dependency versions.
# Without it, npm install resolves latest-compatible versions which can produce
# different build output (especially for vite-plugin-electron and esbuild).
yarn.lock

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
pip-log.txt
pip-delete-this-directory.txt

# =======================
# Archive and Compressed Files
# =======================
*.zip
*.tar.gz
*.rar
*.7z


# User modifications to templates
*-customized.*
*-modified.*

# Test files and data
test-data/
sample-data/
mock-data/

# =======================
# PowerShell Specific
# =======================
# PowerShell Gallery modules
PSGetModuleInfo.xml

# PowerShell transcripts
PowerShell_transcript.*

# PowerShell history
ConsoleHost_history.txt

# =======================
# Azure Specific
# =======================
# Azure Resource Manager cache
.azure-cache/

# =======================
# Git Specific
# =======================
# Git backup files
*.orig
*.rej

# Merge conflict files
*.BACKUP.*
*.BASE.*
*.LOCAL.*
*.REMOTE.*


# API keys and endpoints
*api-key*
*endpoint*
*connection-string*

# Personal notes and scratch files
notes.txt
scratch.*
todo.txt
personal-*

# =======================
# Directory-Specific Ignores
# =======================
# Ignore everything in these directories except README files
/private/
/local/
/user-configs/

# DCR-Automation dev directory (for testing)
Azure/CustomDeploymentTemplates/DCR-Automation/dev/

# Integration Solution build artifacts
Cribl-Microsoft_IntegrationSolution/dist/
Cribl-Microsoft_IntegrationSolution/dist-electron/
Cribl-Microsoft_IntegrationSolution/node_modules/
Cribl-Microsoft_IntegrationSolution/packs/

# But keep README files in ignored directories
!README.md
!readme.md
!README.txt

# =======================
# File Size Limits
# =======================
# Large files that shouldn't be in git
*.iso
*.dmg
*.vhd
*.vmdk

# =======================
# Runtime and Execution
# =======================
# PowerShell execution policy bypass artifacts
*.ps1.bak
*.bat.bak

# Execution logs
execution-*.log
run-*.log
deploy-*.log

# Error dumps
*.dmp
*.crash

# =======================
# Comments for Maintainers
# =======================
# This .gitignore is designed to protect:
# 1. Sensitive authentication data
# 2. User-specific configurations
# 3. Generated output files
# 4. Development environment files
# 5. Platform-specific artifacts
# 6. All hidden dot directories
#
# Always review before committing configuration files
# Use template files (.template.json, .example.json) for examples
# The .*/ catch-all above is for editor and tool dot-directories. .github is
# repository configuration and must be tracked - soc-toolkit-ci.yml already is,
# and new workflows were being silently ignored (2026-08-05).
!.github/
